Subject: [PATCH] x9: isolate MT6993 direct-LK bring-up from legacy MMIO

Select OPPO Find X9 only after PE_init_platform initializes SecureDT. Remove
pre-ADT physical drawing and unconditional X676C framebuffer/pstore aliases.
Validate boot video, map only its first frame, and share the larger bounded
console shadow. Persistent logging uses an explicit optional X9 console zone,
Normal-NC memory and a bounded keep-head writer; early messages stay local
until the record can be mapped.

Pet the captured MT6993 TOPRGU watchdog independently of display scanout from
the virtual-timer IRQ. Keep MT6789 and Qualcomm display, accelerator, battery,
UFS and input initialization off on X9. Bound GIC redistributor walking and
account for optional stride/GICR_TYPER.VLPIS. X9 remains CPU0-only.

This is board isolation and a kernel-entry candidate, not hardware evidence
of X9 execution, display scanout, storage, GPU or userland boot.
---
